WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.900 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Our next guest is

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
an Emmy Award-winning
stand-up comedian

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.136 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and an actress you know

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.771 line:92%
from the TV series "Hannibal

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
and films
such as "Ocean's Thirteen"

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:08.041 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and "Victoria &amp; Abdul."

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.876 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her new movie,
"Six Minutes to Midnight,"

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:12.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
comes to theaters and Demand
on March 26th.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:13.747 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So what brings you here,
Mr. Miller?

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:21.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
What sort of Englishman
would accept a post

00:00:21.221 --> 00:00:25.425 size:84% position:42%
teaching Herr Hitler's
League of German Girls?

00:00:25.425 --> 00:00:29.095 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Speaking German ]

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.331 line:92%
-I do not like surprises.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
I will place you
on a trial period.

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome back
to the show Eddie Izzard.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.773 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you?

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm very good.
How are you doing?

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm good.
It's been a very long time

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.045
since you've been here,
seven years, I believe...

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know.
-...and I'm so happy
to have you back.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:49.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I wanted to stay away
for seven years,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.185 align:start size:94% position:6%
as absence makes the heart
grow fonder.

00:00:52.185 --> 00:00:54.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
Something like that.
Yeah.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.389 line:92%
But it seems like yesterday.

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
Didn't we have a chat
at "Saturday Night Live"?

00:00:58.958 --> 00:00:59.826 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We talk together?

00:00:59.826 --> 00:01:01.428 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We have.
Yes, absolutely.

00:01:01.428 --> 00:01:02.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the times
I turned up there.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:05.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah. No, I've been
watching your "Closer Look."

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
I get it. Because I don't know
if your show

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:08.868 align:start size:94% position:6%
totally comes over here
to Britain

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:10.770 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
sometimes bits come over,

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I've been watching it
for ages and then, they said

00:01:13.073 --> 00:01:13.706 size:88% position:44% line:92%
"Hey, come and do that."

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
Great. Excellent.
Fun to talk to you.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:19.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's even nicer when people
who watch the show agree

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
to come on
because most of our guests

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.382 align:start size:94% position:6%
aren't aware
of what we're doing here.

00:01:22.382 --> 00:01:25.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. I see you go in
and you're fighting the fight,

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:29.389
which is great, you know,
because I've got this hat,

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:30.523 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which is...

00:01:30.523 --> 00:01:32.926
And that's what I do
on my marathons and raise money.

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:35.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know where I got "Make
Humanity Great Again" from

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
It just came to me one night
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.198 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I'm like, "Oh, yeah.

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:41.134
I think there's another slogan
like that out there somewhere.

00:01:41.134 --> 00:01:42.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. I think you
got there first.

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.971
I think you got there first.
Now, you mentioned marathons

00:01:44.971 --> 00:01:46.172 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and you're not being --

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:48.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
This isn't just,
"I ran a marathon, ha ha ha.

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:50.009 line:92%
You have just finished --

00:01:50.009 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we've talked about thi
in the past.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've just finished
32 marathons in 31 days,

00:01:56.983 --> 00:01:58.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
which, obviously --

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:02.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
You raised ££200,000,
which is amazing.

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:06.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
But just talk us through how
you even go about that.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:08.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I've got to say I did more.
A third of a million,

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:09.996 size:78% position:39% line:92%
we got to, ££333,000.

00:02:09.996 --> 00:02:12.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
and George Clooney
was counting it down.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically, I was doing it
on a treadmill.

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:16.636 line:92%
You know, it's COVID lockdown,

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:18.638 size:81% position:41%
so, yeah, every day,
I was doing a marathon

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
and doing a stand-up gig
at the end,

00:02:20.006 --> 00:02:21.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is kind of crazy,
but, you know,

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:23.510 size:84% position:42% line:92%
you try to raise money.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:24.711 line:92%
I've done a few of these before,

00:02:24.711 --> 00:02:26.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was talking to peopl
for six hours.

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:28.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, you do your show,
you talk to people.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:30.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was doing six hours of thi
every day,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.719 align:start size:94% position:6%
chatting to people
and running on a thing,

00:02:32.719 --> 00:02:34.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
which actually was good for me
because it was

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:37.157 size:84% position:42%
so mindlessly boring,
running on a treadmill.

00:02:37.157 --> 00:02:39.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I do this.
I raise money.

00:02:39.559 --> 00:02:42.762 size:84% position:42%
You know, I want to be
a member of parliament.

00:02:42.762 --> 00:02:43.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, meanwhile,
I'm doing my film

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Six Minutes to Midnight,"
in which I do a lot of running

00:02:46.599 --> 00:02:49.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
But Make Humanity Great Agai
is my slogan

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:50.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it includes
all Americans in it.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
People say, "That's not good
for America."

00:02:52.972 --> 00:02:54.641 line:92%
No, Americans are in humanity.

00:02:54.641 --> 00:02:56.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
Everyone's included,
7.8 billion.

00:02:56.776 --> 00:02:59.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
And George Clooney
was counting down the number

00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:02.415
as we did the last
double marathon on the last day.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:04.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it was a beautiful thin
to do, kind of crazy.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you did a double maratho
the last day.

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:07.921 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And I will say,

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:11.024
it all sounds impossible,
but, as you mentioned,

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
it strikes me as so much harde
on a treadmill

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
than it would be
in the great outdoors.

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For the brain,
it's just mind-bogglingly --

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:22.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
I thought we would talk to two
or three people a day.

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:24.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
As soon as I got going on this
I said,

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:25.605 line:92%
"Just line the people up.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
I need to talk."
Talk about anything --

00:03:27.307 --> 00:03:29.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
cats and dogs and trees
and helicopters --

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:33.413
to get my mind off this endles
pounding and not going anywhere.

00:03:33.413 --> 00:03:35.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, so,
it was good, in the end.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I talked to some
wonderful people.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, you know, the people
you're raising the money for i

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
for charities all
around the world.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:45.458 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, yeah, it was
a beautiful thing to do.

00:03:45.458 --> 00:03:47.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just kind of bonkers
and out there,

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:48.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
so I do this stuff.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.262 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You shared with us.

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.463 line:92%
This was in The Guardian,

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.599 align:start size:94% position:6%
which, you really have
taken away

00:03:52.599 --> 00:03:55.001 line:92%
the marathon bragging rights

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:56.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
Basically, we have a character
here, saying,

00:03:56.803 --> 00:03:59.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Will you sponsor me
for my marathon?"

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.139 line:92%
"But you only ran the one.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:02.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, "Damn you,
Eddie Izzard!

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:04.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've spoilt it for everyone!
And I think

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:06.112 size:78% position:39%
most marathon runners
would probably say

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:09.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you have effectively
spoilt it.

00:04:09.449 --> 00:04:11.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have, a little bit,
but other people

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:12.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
have done as well.
My dad cut that

00:04:12.652 --> 00:04:14.587 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of The Guardian
newspaper in Britain

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.390
and he put it next to my bed
when I came home to visit him,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
so that's kind of nice.
My dad.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.860 size:84% position:42%
I thought my dad wasn't
really into my career,

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.263
but he seemed to collect
everything from my career.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:26.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, so marathon running
is something I can do.

00:04:26.566 --> 00:04:28.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, if you are
a trans person, as you know,

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
you said actress there
[indistinct]

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:31.971 size:75% position:38% line:92%
but I'm gender fluid

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
and this is a male role
that I've played.

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:35.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been out for 36 years
but people suddenly

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
sort of noticed it,
which is a bit weird.

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:39.779
Like, "Oh, you're suddenly tall!
What?

00:04:39.779 --> 00:04:41.180 line:92%
You didn't give us any notice.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:42.215 line:92%
Thirty-six years' notice, guys

00:04:42.215 --> 00:04:44.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
So everyone -- It's great.
Thank you so much.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a great honor
to be promoted,

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.720 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm pretty fluid.
I see in boy mode

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.323 align:start size:94% position:6%
and girl mode,
like a superhero thing.

00:04:50.323 --> 00:04:51.491 line:92%
That's how I see transgender

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I can be either one
or the other

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:55.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, this film,
"Six Minutes to Midnight,"

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:58.665 size:81% position:41%
is set in the hometown
where my dad grew up

00:04:58.665 --> 00:05:01.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I grew up,
in this girls' school.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:04.504
Judi Dench plays the woman
running this girls' school

00:05:04.504 --> 00:05:08.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is full of the daughters
of the Nazi High Command,

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:09.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and goddaughters.

00:05:09.676 --> 00:05:10.677 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Himmler's goddaughter

00:05:10.677 --> 00:05:11.511 line:92%
was actually at this school,

00:05:11.511 --> 00:05:14.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a seaside town in England
learning English,

00:05:14.681 --> 00:05:16.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
these German girls used
to hang out

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:20.586
with the other right-wing people
in the British aristocracy

00:05:20.586 --> 00:05:22.388 line:92%
Edward VIII was very into Hitler

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.123 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you'll probably know
this kind of history.

00:05:24.123 --> 00:05:26.893 size:78% position:39%
So I didn't even know
this was the truth,

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:29.028 size:75% position:38%
but the school badge
had a British flag

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:31.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a Nazi flag on it
and I thought,

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Whoa!
There's a film in that."

00:05:32.532 --> 00:05:34.133 align:start size:94% position:6%
So the basis of the story
is true --

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
real girls at this school
doing this stuff --

00:05:36.202 --> 00:05:38.638 size:88% position:44%
and then, we've written
a thriller on top of it,

00:05:38.638 --> 00:05:41.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
Judi Dench, myself,
and Jim Broadbent.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, you are
a very accomplished writer

00:05:43.343 --> 00:05:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you had never written
a screenplay before.

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:46.879 line:92%
Did you find it daunting?

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:48.748 line:92%
Did you enjoy that process

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.982 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. You were talking
to Amy Poehler.

00:05:49.982 --> 00:05:51.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
She said don't do writing,
you know, this thing.

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.053 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because you're obviously
a wildly experienced writer,

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:56.422 size:84% position:42%
but, you know, I come
from where you've lived

00:05:56.422 --> 00:05:58.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of your life,
that shorter sketch thing?

00:05:58.791 --> 00:06:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
I came from sketch.
Then I went to stand-up.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had to learn
a whole new different thing.

00:06:02.462 --> 00:06:03.996 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I couldn't do stand-up.

00:06:03.996 --> 00:06:06.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
I broke into Pinewood Studio
when I was 15.

00:06:06.065 --> 00:06:08.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Steven Spielberg, I think,
worked at Universal

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:09.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
when he was
about 17, 18, you know,

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.571 size:78% position:39%
so I was trying to do
this similar thing.

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:13.673 line:92%
He got his career going bam!

00:06:13.673 --> 00:06:14.374 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And mine took

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
30, 40 years, you know.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.209 --> 00:06:18.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
The fine-wine approach
to careers.

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:20.313
Because I knew I didn't know
how to do story structure,

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.816 align:start size:94% position:6%
character --
I didn't have the sense of it,

00:06:23.816 --> 00:06:25.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I wrote
with two other writers.

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:27.253 size:81% position:41%
And this has obviously
got a powerful thing

00:06:27.253 --> 00:06:29.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
because like the message was
from the 1930s

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:31.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then, you had this thing
particularly in America,

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:35.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
you got Brexit,
you've got Trump,

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:35.795 size:84% position:42% line:92%
the same kind of thing.

00:06:35.795 --> 00:06:37.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
You've got the
Alternative for Deutschlan

00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:40.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
in Germany again,
and Marine Le Pen,

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
all this right-wing thinking
around the world,

00:06:42.135 --> 00:06:43.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is like going back
to the 1930s,

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:47.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we're trying
to drag the world to the 2030s

00:06:47.073 --> 00:06:48.040 line:92%
and say, "Let's move forward."

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
And some people, it's like
"No, let's go back.

00:06:49.308 --> 00:06:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's have another go
at the 1930s.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.512 line:92%
How did it turn out last time?

00:06:52.512 --> 00:06:53.679 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:55.915 size:88% position:44%
Our film has, hopefully,
got a message in there

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.551
that is, you know, "If you
do not learn from history,

00:06:58.551 --> 00:06:59.786 line:92%
you're doomed to repeat it."

00:06:59.786 --> 00:07:03.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, now, more than ever,
it's just resonating.

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:07.093 align:start size:94% position:6%
And our film sits there, right
on the eve of World War II

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:09.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
